{
  "name": "CV Screening — Prototype (JD + CVs in one form)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=<goal>\nConvert the job description below into a structured, auditable list of evaluation criteria. Do NOT score any candidate. Do NOT add requirements that are not stated or clearly implied by the JD.\n</goal>\n\n<job_description>\n{{ $json.body['Job Description'] }}\n</job_description>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Extract CORE requirements (must-haves): things a candidate cannot lack.\n2. Extract PREFERRED qualifications (nice-to-haves / bonuses).\n3. Give each requirement:\n   - a short stable id (\"c1\",\"c2\"... for core; \"p1\",\"p2\"... for preferred)\n   - a one-line \"requirement\" phrased as a checkable criterion\n   - a \"weight\" from 1 (minor) to 3 (critical), reflecting how central it is\n4. Keep each requirement atomic — one skill/qualification per item. Split compound requirements (\"React and TypeScript\") into separate items.\n5. If the JD is empty or is not a job description, return empty arrays.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nReturn ONLY this JSON object, no prose:\n{\n  \"core_requirements\": [ { \"id\": \"c1\", \"requirement\": \"<string>\", \"weight\": <1-3> } ],\n  \"preferred\":         [ { \"id\": \"p1\", \"requirement\": \"<string>\", \"weight\": <1-3> } ]\n}\n</output_format>",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You extract structured hiring criteria from a job description. You do not invent requirements that are not present. You separate non-negotiable Core Requirements from nice-to-have Preferred Qualifications, and you assign each an importance weight from 1 to 3. You output only JSON."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
