      "id": "7051f19f-626b-48ba-86ea-079b66ff64b5",
      "name": "Attach criteria"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=<goal>\nFor EACH criterion in <criteria>, decide whether the candidate's CV provides evidence that it is met, partially met, or not met. Cite the evidence. Do not compute or output any overall score — that is done elsewhere.\n</goal>\n\n<criteria>\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.criteria) }}\n</criteria>\n\n<candidate_cv>\n{{ $json.extractedText }}\n</candidate_cv>\n\n<rules>\n- Judge ONLY on text explicitly present in the CV. Do not infer or assume.\n- \"met\"     = the CV clearly and directly satisfies the criterion.\n- \"partial\" = the CV touches the criterion but weakly, ambiguously, or without the depth/duration the criterion asks for.\n- \"not_met\" = the CV provides no evidence for the criterion.\n- \"evidence\" MUST be a short verbatim snippet quoted from the CV (<= 25 words), or null. If evidence is null, verdict CANNOT be \"met\".\n- Reason in one short sentence per criterion.\n- Lean toward \"partial\" (not \"not_met\") when the candidate clearly works in the right domain but the exact phrasing is absent — do not hard-drop adjacent or transferable experience.\n- If the CV text is empty or is clearly not a resume, set \"cv_quality\" to \"unreadable\" and mark every verdict \"not_met\".\n</rules>\n\n<output_format>\nReturn ONLY this JSON object, no prose:\n{\n  \"cv_quality\": \"ok\" | \"unreadable\",\n  \"verdicts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"<criterion id, matching the input>\",\n      \"verdict\": \"met\" | \"partial\" | \"not_met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"<verbatim CV snippet, or null>\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"<one sentence>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</output_format>",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are a CV evaluation assistant. You judge a candidate's CV against a fixed list of criteria. For each criterion you decide: met, partial, or not_met, and you cite the exact CV text that justifies it. You judge ONLY on what the CV explicitly states — you never assume or infer skills that are not written. You output only JSON. You do not output a score or a rating."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
